# AGENTS.md — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

A static site generated from Swift with [WingedSwift](https://github.com/micheltlutz/Winged-Swift).
Read this before changing anything.

## How this project works

`swift run` executes `Sources/{{PROJECT_NAME}}/main.swift`. It declares the site as a `Site` and
calls `publish()`, which renders every `Page` through the layout and writes `dist/` — pages,
assets, `404.html`, `sitemap.xml` and `robots.txt`. There is no server and no runtime: everything
happens at build time.

```
Sources/{{PROJECT_NAME}}/
├── main.swift          # the Site: name, URL, pages, layout — and publish()
├── Pages.swift         # one `Page` type per page
├── SiteLayout.swift    # the shell shared by every page (head extras, nav, footer)
└── Components.swift    # content data + reusable markup
assets/                 # css/js/images copied into dist/
dist/                   # generated — do not edit by hand
```

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `winged build` | Generates the site into `dist/`. |
| `winged serve --watch` | Serves `dist/` on http://localhost:8000 and rebuilds on change. |
| `swift build` | Type-checks without generating. |

## Rules

1. **Never edit `dist/`.** It is overwritten on every build. Change the Swift source.
2. **Never invent a tag type.** Check the
   [tag catalog](https://github.com/micheltlutz/Winged-Swift/blob/main/.claude/skills/wingedswift/references/tag-catalog.md);
   if an element has no type, use `HTMLTag("element-name") { … }` or `RawHTML("<svg …>")`.
3. **Content is escaped by default.** Pass raw text — never pre-escape. `escapeContent: false` is
   only for markup you generated yourself.
4. **Add a page** by declaring a `struct … : Page` in `Pages.swift` (a `title` and a `body`; the
   path comes from the type name, `Pricing` → `/pricing/`) and listing it in `pages` in
   `main.swift`. Do not add `<title>` or SEO meta tags — `publish()` writes them from the page.
   Set `url` in `main.swift` to the real domain before deploying; canonical links and the sitemap
   use it.
5. **Add a section or card** as a `struct … : Component` with a `body` in `Components.swift`
   (a `static func … -> HTMLTag` works too), then use it in a page. Keep the copy in
   `Content`, not inline in the markup.
6. **Style with classes**, chained: `.addClass("card")`, `.addClasses(["grid", "gap-4"])`. Edit the
   CSS in `assets/css/`.

## Upgrading WingedSwift

Read [MIGRATION.md](https://github.com/micheltlutz/Winged-Swift/blob/main/MIGRATION.md) for the
target version and follow the
[`wingedswift-migrate` skill](https://github.com/micheltlutz/Winged-Swift/blob/main/.claude/skills/wingedswift-migrate/SKILL.md):
snapshot `dist/`, bump the dependency, apply the documented rewrites, rebuild, and diff `dist/`
against the snapshot before committing.

## Before you say you are done

```bash
winged build
```

Then open `dist/index.html` and confirm the change is actually in the generated HTML — a build that
succeeds is not proof the page looks right.
